{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done","id":1509297,"title":"Old World of Darkness is officially done","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-22T10:19:20-07:00","id":1509297,"title":"Old World of Darkness is officially done","content":"With the W5 preview outright saying that the edition is a full on &quot;reimagination&quot; (aka Reboot), heralds in the fact that oWoD as we know it, is officially done. They at least tried to keep a low semblance of continuity in V5 (even with how poor that was within itself), but then we started to the cracks with H5..<br /> <br /> The Imbued removed? I was severely disappointed and angered by that, but then thought they only did so because Parawolf knew that HtR had a relatively small fanbase, so push-back would be minimal. Coupled with the fact that Parawolf seems to be on a crusade to excise anything remotely interesting, that does not fit the certain one-note linear pathway they've set oWoD on, making the Imbued more generic and have little to do with metaplot was a sure thing, considering their modus operandi. H5 also was not one the big three (VtM, WtA, &amp; MtA).<br /> <br /> ..But now with what they're doing in WtA? It's full-on clear that Parawolf does not care about any true vestige of oWoD; like what's been said over-and-over again ad nauseum by many people on this site; is that Parawolf only cares about the convenient branding power oWoD has, but cares little about what made the games enjoyable and loved by the former community of oWoD players (and I say former, in the sense that Parawolf is clearly trying to appeal to entirely another niche audience). <br /> <br /> The 20th gamelines are basically the unofficial-official last &quot;true editions&quot; (for better or worse, if for some reason you don't like the 20th editions - I particularly don't like WtO 20th and stick with 2ed) of old World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T18:54:58-07:00","id":1509336,"title":"","content":"There's a V5 out there? I really wasn't paying attention. I've been through to many editions between the various games we play, it doesn't matter. If I happen across a V5-book, I'll read it and take any rule or idea I like and apply it to 2nd. <br /> <br /> Look at the bright-side, did they use pictures of dressed up Barbie-dolls in the book like Cyberpunk V3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T19:56:39-07:00","id":1509343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509336#post1509336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look at the bright-side, did they use pictures of dressed up Barbie-dolls in the book like Cyberpunk V3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse, the books are full of truly....discutable larp like pictures.<br /> oh, and they threw in a load of the concept arts for the cancelled world of darkness mmo. For reasons that reason ignores","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T00:56:07-07:00","id":1509355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509336#post1509336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a V5 out there? I really wasn't paying attention. I've been through to many editions between the various games we play, it doesn't matter. If I happen across a V5-book, I'll read it and take any rule or idea I like and apply it to 2nd.<br /> <br /> Look at the bright-side, did they use pictures of dressed up Barbie-dolls in the book like Cyberpunk V3?</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is... divisive. It brings in ideas from Requiem, depowers the Camarilla, shuffles the Sabbat off to one side, returns to the Camarilla Seven in the corebook and the others in supplements, and a couple of big changes to the status quo that you'll either find fine or utterly hate (government hunters being formalised into the Second Inquisition, the fall of the Tremere, the hacking of SHRECKnet and subsequent technophobic Camarilla). The good changes (e.g. Nosferatu no longer being inherently Masquerade breaking) are balanced out by the bad (e.g. Nosferatu no longer looking like a shaved gibbon baked at 2000 Kelvin's and stuck in a trenchcoat*).<br /> <br /> And by 'take stuff from Requiem' I mean stuff like weaker kindred and Blood Potency. Generally things that don't really fit with the themes of Masquerade, but people or the Devs liked in Requiem.<br /> <br /> * I mean, I think they're supposed to look ugly, but their actual bane is now a Requiem style unease caused in mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T07:25:43-07:00","id":1509374,"title":"","content":"It looks like we're heading for a fanbase schism as the company makes so many sweeping changes to their intended new edition that it becomes unpalatable to many of their old fans.<br /> <br /> I feel like I've seen this before, something about backlash for the dev's chosen interpretation of the end times and a new world of darkness.<br /> <br /> That can't be right though, Surely a major company that's invested millions in acquiring an IP would research their history and not repeat the mistakes that put that IP up for sale in the first place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T09:45:27-07:00","id":1509387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509374#post1509374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks like we're heading for a fanbase schism as the company makes so many sweeping changes to their intended new edition that it becomes unpalatable to many of their old fans.<br /> <br /> That can't be right though, Surely a major company that's invested millions in acquiring an IP would research their history and not repeat the mistakes that put that IP up for sale in the first place...</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually they go by the rule of more and &quot;better&quot; plus &quot;I don't want to be sued&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T10:42:10-07:00","id":1509397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509355#post1509355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 is... divisive. It brings in ideas from Requiem, depowers the Camarilla, shuffles the Sabbat off to one side, returns to the Camarilla Seven in the corebook and the others in supplements, and a couple of big changes to the status quo that you'll either find fine or utterly hate (government hunters being formalised into the Second Inquisition, the fall of the Tremere, the hacking of SHRECKnet and subsequent technophobic Camarilla). The good changes (e.g. Nosferatu no longer being inherently Masquerade breaking) are balanced out by the bad (e.g. Nosferatu no longer looking like a shaved gibbon baked at 2000 Kelvin's and stuck in a trenchcoat*).<br /> <br /> And by 'take stuff from Requiem' I mean stuff like weaker kindred and Blood Potency. Generally things that don't really fit with the themes of Masquerade, but people or the Devs liked in Requiem.<br /> <br /> * I mean, I think they're supposed to look ugly, but their actual bane is now a Requiem style unease caused in mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requiem vampires are way stronger than those of V20. Also their game mechanics is the best from any vampire games.<br /> <br /> Unlike V5 requiem reacted to the fan base criticism and corrected the bad stuff from their 1ED core like the fog of ages and the like. 2ED is no longer a shadow of the masquerade but a game on his own. They are not comparable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T11:16:19-07:00","id":1509400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509397#post1509397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Requiem vampires are way stronger than those of V20. Also their game mechanics is the best from any vampire games.<br /> <br /> Unlike V5 requiem reacted to the fan base criticism and corrected the bad stuff from their 1ED core like the fog of ages and the like. 2ED is no longer a shadow of the masquerade but a game on his own. They are not comparable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I specifically meant pathetic 1e Requiem vampires, where Vigor let you add your dots in it to your strength rating for 1 Vitae/scene. I think Fortitude was just extra Health boxes for the same cost. They were just pathetic, Requiem 2e is just massively better than the first edition was, mostly by running in the directions V5 didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T11:42:24-07:00","id":1509401,"title":"","content":"Ehhh, maybe? The cruch will be how well w5 does. If it undersells then they may reconsider their position. It does well then full steam ahead.<br /> <br /> it occurs to me its not particularly clear why they think hypothetical new fans would find their new spin on the setting preferable, especially if they establish a rep as not respecting their own customers/fans which they're well on the way to doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T15:10:50-07:00","id":1509412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509401#post1509401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhh, maybe? The cruch will be how well w5 does. If it undersells then they may reconsider their position. It does well then full steam ahead.<br /> <br /> it occurs to me its not particularly clear why they think hypothetical new fans would find their new spin on the setting preferable, especially if they establish a rep as not respecting their own customers/fans which they're well on the way to doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time, people don't take company history as a parameter, this is a minority, also from what I understand the idea is that new games are made simpler so that new players have less to read and memorize, that's how they took some disciplines, and put everything that is necromancer inside the Hecata clan, that even makes sense, but it leaves me with a bad taste in my mouth in some parts, it seems that some clans have lost their identity. Also I tried playing a few sessions of Requiem and it was a mess so I'm kind of afraid to try again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T21:30:24-07:00","id":1509443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509412#post1509412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the time, people don't take company history as a parameter, this is a minority, also from what I understand the idea is that new games are made simpler so that new players have less to read and memorize, that's how they took some disciplines, and put everything that is necromancer inside the Hecata clan, that even makes sense, but it leaves me with a bad taste in my mouth in some parts, it seems that some clans have lost their identity. Also I tried playing a few sessions of Requiem and it was a mess so I'm kind of afraid to try again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not so much company history as company rep. EA for example has a bad rep and this is embedded in gaming cultureI. I think their model of accesability is a failure, when you look at the disciplines they're not actually simpler theirs just less of then and individual disciplines are more complex, with combo powers, alternative lineups and blood alchemy using a differant rule set.<br /> <br /> Clan identity loss is more about their disdain of clans as culture and desire to treat them as a character class which ultimately makes them bland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 04-24-2023, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T00:00:44-07:00","id":1509457,"title":"","content":"Company history also as to be considered in the arena that company operates in. The more niche a product is, the more the company matters, because the more you need to keep a dedicated fan-base to keep buying over and over. Companies with broader appeal can risk far more alienation of old fans because that broad appeal means they have a large pool of new customers to pull in.<br /> <br /> There's also a scale issue. Small companies are easier for consumers to relate to; which cuts both ways. If there are 10 scumbags working at a company of 50 people, most people are going to naturally be very wary of that company in general because it's a small enough group that we'll think of them as a community of humans. If there are 10 scumbags in a company of 50,000 people, it becomes a situation our brains don't engage with and we'll write it off as there always being a few bad apples/etc. We're just not wired to see individuals in a crowd that big; esp. not from the outside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T07:38:23-07:00","id":1509476,"title":"","content":"In my experience the &quot;scumbags&quot; are usually where it counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:58:44-07:00","id":1509508,"title":"","content":"I mean, if they want to explore an reimagining or alternative universe or whatever I'd be quite happy to give that a shot. I do actually like V5 for what it and would be willing to try out the other two except that they've strangled oWoD and CofD in the process, so fuck 'em. <br /> On the plus side, listening to fans of WoD gamelines I've always dismissed passionately arguing in said lines' defence has inspired me to actually take a look at them.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Also looking forward to/dreading the next WoD5 games. Observing hardcore mage fans is going to be schadenfreude (and as someone who enjoys the Technocracy, I don't need any faqs or previews to know I'll be told to get fucked) and Changeling and Wraith are probably going to make me froth at the mouth and start tearing my hair out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T23:07:21-07:00","id":1509691,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't hold my breath on Wraith or Changeling getting a 5th Edition makeover. My impression is that neither line sold well enough to be worth these multimedia/videogames companies' time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T00:28:03-07:00","id":1509693,"title":"","content":"I also don't expect a fan backlash to change Parawolf's strategy as long as people keep buying the books (seemingly mostly to complain about them). There's no noticeable difference between a happy and unhappy purchase in the sales data.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm planning to buy W5, but it's also the first WoD5 purchase I'll have made since V5's Anarch and Camarilla (disappointing, I actually mostly liked the core book). I also might pick up the other V5 books at some point, but I also liked the general direction of V5 after some basic houserules (i.e. fixing Generation and Hunger). But I've not pre-ordered it, because they're not getting my money until I'm fully certain it'll be interesing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T06:16:50-07:00","id":1509709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509691#post1509691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't hold my breath on Wraith or Changeling getting a 5th Edition makeover. My impression is that neither line sold well enough to be worth these multimedia/videogames companies' time.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they did release a Wraith VR game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T06:47:19-07:00","id":1509713,"title":"","content":"To myself, it doesn't really matter if something has been officially dead or unofficially dead for any stretch of time. People still play DnD 3.5 and Pathfinder 1e, I also know some eldritch creatures that still play DnD 1e. The TTRPG necromancy will always happen and be a thing as long as people are willing to look around and not just play the new things for being new. I have introduced a lot of players to the x20 lines and will probably continue to use that as my base for the games and stories that I want to tell in WoD.<br /> <br /> The question of &quot;Will x5 be the death of WOD?&quot; Has a real answer and a real <i>real</i> answer. The real answer is probably not, not only has the releases so far been <i>ok</i> in sales as far as we have seen but, I don't think Paradox would just buy the IP and not try to make their money back from it at least. The real <i>real</i> answer is that it doesn't matter, I'm not there target demographic and even if they made a new edition or continue with x5, I can't imagine it to be anything appealing to me. I might be surprised but, I'm not holding my breath.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:44:00-07:00","id":1509764,"title":"","content":"There's always the possibility of reconciliation. Just look at what happened with New Coke and Coca-Cola Classic back in the 80s and 90s. Coke tried to come up with something new to gain market share. It brought in new buyers, but alienated older ones, causing a loss in market share anyway. Coke brought the original version back as Classic, and ultimately would fold New Coke, but not before reconfiguring Classic a little since then. The same could happen with the WOD. There is a way to bring about many of the changes to W5 without doing away with the previous meta plot as well as keeping many of the original mechanics so many of the older players loved. I've been trying to work on it ever since the first hints of W5 came out last year. There is always a chance something like that could happen here, especially if the IP changes hands again. In fact, I've been working on a whole analogy to the cola wars of the time to how the handling of the WOD IP is today. There are quite a few parallels once I started a deep dive into it, but I don't know if anyone here is ready for a lengthy discussion of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T13:37:37-07:00","id":1509778,"title":"","content":"The Cola Wars was kinda beating-a-dead-horse issue thanks to the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness now Chronicles of Darkness debates.<br /> <br /> The big problem is that, as you indicate, reconciliation would probably require the IP changing hands again. Paradox has invested a lot of money in these IPs (both the upfront purchase, new hires, buying up smaller gaming studios to build up a team better suited to WoD video games, etc.) to the point where basically no TTRPG focused company can afford a price they'd want to clear their ledgers. It would have to be a larger entertainment company, which is unlikely to be good for reconciliation unless they do what CCP eventually did and just let Onyx Path handle it as a trusted company regarding both the legacy of the games and trying to do new stuff with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T06:31:20-07:00","id":1509857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509778#post1509778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Paradox has invested a lot of money in these IPs (both the upfront purchase, new hires, buying up smaller gaming studios to build up a team better suited to WoD video games, etc.) to the point where basically no TTRPG focused company can afford a price they'd want to clear their ledgers. It would have to be a larger entertainment company, which is unlikely to be good for reconciliation unless they do what CCP eventually did and just let Onyx Path handle it as a trusted company regarding both the legacy of the games and trying to do new stuff with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I would be surprised if TTRPG book sales are anywhere near what Paradox brings in from video games. If anything comes from Bloodlines 2 or either of VtM or Exalted TV/Media developments work out, it'll pretty much guarantee ParadWolf isn't going to let the IP go. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T06:55:18-07:00","id":1509859,"title":"","content":"Hell, Night Road basically sold me on V5 as a viable game, if a different one to earlier editions or Requiem. It's a bit of a shame that everything good in WoD computer games has been a text adventure or visual novel, they just don't have the reach that other genres do. I'm also still shocked at the lack of new novels, but maybe it's time to hit up Forbidden Planet for a comics omnibus.<br /> <br /> Outside of the mainstream WoD5 hasn't been ridiculously successful, although it's probably had enough solid hits to not be considered a waste. Unfortunately it's more mainstream stuff has been disappointing, something something Earthblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the same time my opinion of the W5 previews flips between 'this is going to be shit' and 'maybe it'll work when I see everything together'. I've accepted that neoWoD is going to be it's own thing and try to judge it on it's merits, but it's hard to mentally separate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T07:09:51-07:00","id":1509860,"title":"","content":"Seeing what has been done with W5 part of me is thankful that WtF isn't getting any new books, but on the other hand, if it does as I suspect and hope it does, perhaps that will open the door for CofD to get a green light for new books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T11:34:17-07:00","id":1509873,"title":"","content":"What really frustrates me is parawolfs antipathy towards the fans and how aggressively the fandom has been split 3 ways now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:28:17-07:00","id":1509878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509859#post1509859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, Night Road basically sold me on V5 as a viable game, if a different one to earlier editions or Requiem. It's a bit of a shame that everything good in WoD computer games has been a text adventure or visual novel, they just don't have the reach that other genres do. I'm also still shocked at the lack of new novels, but maybe it's time to hit up Forbidden Planet for a comics omnibus.<br /> <br /> Outside of the mainstream WoD5 hasn't been ridiculously successful, although it's probably had enough solid hits to not be considered a waste. Unfortunately it's more mainstream stuff has been disappointing, something something Earthblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the same time my opinion of the W5 previews flips between 'this is going to be shit' and 'maybe it'll work when I see everything together'. I've accepted that neoWoD is going to be it's own thing and try to judge it on it's merits, but it's hard to mentally separate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't that go wrong with Sins of Sirs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-27T12:44:00-07:00","id":1509882,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the fan base isn't as 3-way split as it could be. Pre-5e cWoD fans and CofD fans might not be buying the same books, but are generally more united by not liking Paradox's dismissive attitude towards them as fans and customers than they used to be divided around gaming preferences. The period where 20th books and CofD 2e books were both getting good support at the same time also helped, because it was clear we can all coexist without it feeling like someone had to get less games/books so someone else could get the games/books they wanted (which was definitely a problem when the nWoD was used as a flat replacement for the cWoD back in '04).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T07:03:42-07:00","id":1509955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509857#post1509857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. I would be surprised if TTRPG book sales are anywhere near what Paradox brings in from video games. If anything comes from <b>Bloodlines 2</b> or either of VtM or Exalted TV/Media developments work out, it'll pretty much guarantee ParadWolf isn't going to let the IP go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incredibly unlikely for the same reason that warner brothers is unlikely to salvage the DC cinematic universe. There's so much mismanagement, conflicting artistic visions, and corporate drama storms surrounding the non-tabletop parts of WOD right now that they're most likely going to lose money.<br /> <br /> WOD is a fantastic IP, but parawolf is seriously messing up it's chances to attract new fans in other markets while simultaneously complicating it's relationship with old fans. I wouldn't be surprised if, in 5 years, paradox puts up the WOD IPs for sale for pennies on the dollar(like marvel did before they were eaten by sony and disney) just to make Something back.<br /> <br /> This isn't helped by the fact america's market is heading for hard times in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-28T09:15:20-07:00","id":1509960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509878#post1509878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't that go wrong with Sins of Sirs?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text adventures have been going downhill since Our For Blood (which I personally like). The visual novels seem to have improved with Shadows of New York and Heart of the Forest. Unfortunately both kinds of games are almost entirely dependent on the skills of the author, so who knows how the next ones will turn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T19:31:27-07:00","id":1510305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1509397#post1509397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . .the fog of ages. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the fog of ages; it makes sense with the epistemology-classes I took. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T08:19:53-07:00","id":1510601,"title":"","content":"I for one am puzzled by all these absurdly solid IPs getting mostly bad entries. No universe has ever engrossed me so completely as WoD has, conveying simple universal truths through monstrous exaggerations. Between WoD and whatever the fuck is going on with DC and Star Wars gets me deeply conspiratorial. Like how could they possibly go so awry? Are they doing it on purpose for some political reason? Has <i>Star Wars</i> been made a leftist caricature to push people to the right? Is WoD pulling it's punches because it used to be such an amazing satirical engine that targeted real problems? Is Henry Cavill cursed? <br /> <br /> With things like Bethesda Game Studios failing to live up to TES and Fallout I can at least justify it with video games being extremely complicated and difficult to make and the lore taking a back seat for gameplay and spectacle seems to at least be a financially viable tactic, even if I don't agree with it. TV and movies cost a lot of money and producers are a difficult demon to keep at bay so it's understandable that things can get messy. But with WoD like... it's a fucking book. The risk of such a book is minimal, especially given us young folk like digital copies, so that kind of studio meddling should be unwarranted. Put me on the keyboard and give me enough wages to convince the wife I'm doing one of those so-called &quot;real&quot; jobs, grab me someone to draw the pictures and arrange pages and we'll shit something out much better than what we're currently getting. I'm not especially competent; I just recognize the bar is low. I'd trust half the regulars on this forum to write an improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T22:41:32-07:00","id":1510677,"title":"","content":"Honestly, now that I've come back to think about it again, I can't help but feel bitter about what's going on with oWoD nowadays. <br /> <br /> I tried not to not be... but I can't, because oWoD was so unique and just awesome; even despite some of the &quot;choicier&quot; material found within it. Parawolf overcorrecting and then stuffing it with even worse material that is completely bland and doesn't match any theme or internal logic that the previous edition of a certain game had, is just utterly horrible.<br /> <br /> All the things they're doing to WtA SHOULD not the happening.. and I'm shocked that they're doing this &quot;reimaging&quot; thing (see: reboot) with WtA to begin with, as it was one of the &quot;Big Three&quot; of White Wolf splats. Hell, Parawolf doesn't even give WtA the courtesy of at least being a &quot;soft-reboot&quot; like what they did with V5... just trash the entire setting and make it more like another game series, because you got mad the former wasn't as popular as the classic predecessor. <br /> <br /> To be completely honest, Parawolf should have just stuck with developing CofD games and left it at that, to let oWoD die peacefully. It's clear that they don't genuinely care about the majority of aspects that made oWoD.... oWoD. But again, to beat a dead bush, they've done this strategy for pure branding power, and nothing else.<br /> <br /> All the changes they make, when it's not something to make oWoD to be more like CofD, is to either remove something that they think modern sensibilities and nu-young adult audiences cannot &quot;handle&quot; for some reason (even though WoD in general is supposed to explore mature themes, with urban fantasy mixed-in; i.e Metis and Kinfolk for the Garou being removed, thus eliminating any context to how Garou integrated with humans throughout the ages or formed their own subcultures within already existing human ones... this was a deliberate design choice); or something that the nu-writers at Parawolf have a clear bias for or against:<br /> <br /> <b>VTM</b><br /> <br /> - Anarchs being a sudden uber faction, when they were always the peripheral third faction (clearly someone at Parawolf is an Anarch fan of somesort)<br /> <br /> - A dumb Beckoning plot devise to remove all the Elders from the game, thus enforcing more street level and angsty disorganized Vampire society, instead of the high-stakes supernatural political maneuvering and intrigue that was the old feel of the game<br /> <br /> - The Sabbat being completely removed from the game as playable characters and lorewise basically all migrating to the Middle-East due to this &quot;Beckoning&quot; plot device nonsense (the most egregious thing Parawolf has done to show their bias against certain elements in the oWoD franchise)<br /> <br /> - Tremere being broken up in the dumbest way possible<br /> <br /> - Lasombra mass defecting to the Camarilla despite the Vinculum and the centuries of fighting against the Camarilla, a sect traditionally associated with their greatest rivals, the Venture (no doubt a meta-bias by someone at Parawolf who leaned toward the &quot;Camarilla Lasombra&quot; camp of yore.. that now has become a cringe-worthy reality)<br /> <br /> - Making the Followers of Set join the Anarchs, when they always were being on the sidelines away from the other sects and corrupting everyone equally. Then afterwards, evangelize (literally in this case) their name to &quot;The Ministry&quot; as way to unsubtly harken-align them to basically be &quot;the Christian megachurch guiss who're actually corrupt from the inside and manipulate people xDDDD&quot;<br /> <br /> - Unique bloodlines being soft deleted by the new &quot;Loresheet&quot; institution introduced by Parawolf, due to the bigotry of low expectation that new people cannot go back to learn about these interesting bloodlines by themselves; so now let's just completely make them one-note (literally) and be something that a newcomer to oWoD will have zero interest in playing them to begin with... <br /> <br /> - All the unique Disciplines have now been relegated to the stupid Amalgam system (the principal casualty of this being Vicissitude) because Parawolf thought that all of these powers would be too much for newcomers to stomach... then they turn around by releasing at least 150~+? Amalgam powers that <i>surely</i> will be more easily consumer to the average person.. oh, and no more Discipline dots above 5; because it was too much &quot;bloat&quot;... but again, the whole 150+ Amalgam powers thing...<br /> <br /> - Whatever the Hecata is supposed to be<br /> <br /> <b>HtR</b><br /> <br /> - The IMBUED.. the key element characters of that entire splat.. being COMPLETELY remove from their own game.. and as far as I know (correct me if I'm wrong) not even mentioned in H5. This is one of the most RIDICULOUS things Parawolf as done.<br /> <br /> <b>WtA</b><br /> <br /> Most of the grievances against the upcoming W5 and the glaring problems that have already arrived with the release of some information of it, can basically be found in the WtA forum. To me, however, the worst thing Parawolf basically did with W5, is making the Umbra DE-EMPHASIZED / relegating to a more &quot;uncharted&quot; status.. no, just no.. It's clear to me they didn't want to deal with the unique cosmology of the Umbra and all of its unique locations, so now they want to make it more like Hisil from WtF (which is clear as day given the attitude of the former design lead). <br /> <br /> Also, something that I touched base with before in this post, is the fact on how the Garou basically.. are nothings now. They have no real culture or are now not supposed to be connected with any context to human society in an alt-history sense at all (except for the Fianna.. because apparently Fianna is just a &quot;word&quot;? As if it has nothing to do with the Celtic peoples? But nah, apparently it <i>is just a word</i>, so it can safely fit in with the idiotic &quot;verb&quot; naming scheme thing Parawolf came up with)<br /> <br /> The only audience W5 is going to have is V5 fans.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I don't expect W5 to do particularly well at all; especially more-so with how the WtA community has reacted to it. I wonder what Parawolf will do if W5 ends up a disaster like H5 was, or if they'll even entertain doing a M5.. which will be the mother-of-all-disasters with how Paradox-Parawolf is handling this franchise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T22:51:15-07:00","id":1510678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510601#post1510601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Henry Cavill cursed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably<br /> But not as severly as <b>Scott Bakula</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T23:57:24-07:00","id":1510685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510677#post1510677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, now that I've come back to think about it again, I can't help but feel bitter about what's going on with oWoD nowadays.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Last night I got around to finishing <i>Wolfenstein: New Order</i>, which had decent gameplay, but the sheer amount of cutscene incompetence frustrated and undermined any sort of impact the narrative was supposed to have. Oh we're getting tortured, well given the bullshit that got us here we probably deserve it. I've mowed down and grappled a thousand soldiers and been shot a hundred times only to be felled by a doctor hiding behind a door, unsafely retrieving an electrical item, or a twink* hiding at the top of a short ladder? Bullshit. Any kind of catharsis I'm supposed to be getting by killing villains is marred by frustration. And so to does V5 handle things: Camarilla? Suddenly falls apart from overacting to an SI it should've been on top of. Anarchs? make big wins because their opponents went full stupid. Brujah? somehow banded together to do the thing the writers always said they wouldn't. Lasombra? Entire sect ran off into the sunset. Get of Fenrir? written off to be a caricature the tribe shunned and avoided. The elders that had us under their boots and who we were always trying to usurp? They just left...<br /> <br /> <i>*Irony points for a game about killing intolerant Nazis doing their best to create disgust towards an effeminate male and his girlboss partner</i>.<br /> <br /> But more frustrating than that is the actual underlying changes to how vampires fundamentally work. Generation used to be something of envy and would drive people to murder, now it's a trap that'll give you hunger issues more than anything else: Vampire is no longer about a parasitic minority doing crazy shit to hold onto and gain power, but about carefully managing your mental health, not succumbing to temptation, and being content with your lot. Unlike the real world where the baby-boomers are still hoarding the senior jobs, the elders of V5 have all chosen to retire.<br /> <br /> Let's not get into fundamentally misunderstanding the beliefs and modus operandi that made the Camarilla, Sabbat, Tremere and Followers of Set so successful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-04-2023, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T09:08:09-07:00","id":1510705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But more frustrating than that is the actual underlying changes to how vampires fundamentally work. Generation used to be something of envy and would drive people to murder, now it's a trap that'll give you hunger issues more than anything else\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also clear that the primary design focus (which has been obvious for years now) is just making all oWoD splats to be more like CofD splats, in regard to you mentioning how Vampires have been changed in this X5th line of games; key in point in how they introduced BLOOD POTENCY of all things... into VtM.. A game about where if you wanted to raise your power ceiling, you HAD to diablerize and plan-out the resulting fallout afterward to survive. <br /> <br /> Making Blood Potency and Generation cohabitate in the same game makes no sense at all. Blood Potency was a tool for CofD to operate WITHOUT Generation, so it could be intrinsically metaplot non-existent; along with de-emphasizing the low-to-high hanging struggle of childer vs sire, or neonate against elder.<br /> <br /> Them adding in Blood Potency to VtM but having to have to leave in Generation, just shows what direction they ultimately want for basically all of the oWoD games at this point. They probably wanted to just remove Generation altogether, but couldn't, since that would break the basic internal logic and bedrock of the game too far; so their next &quot;best&quot; solution was probably to come up with the dumb Beckoning thing to remove the Elders. So now the groundwork fiat FORCES you to be either a neonate or an anchilla, as now elders are (all but basically) unplayable / not present in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T14:27:49-07:00","id":1510718,"title":"","content":"I find the combination of Generation and Blood Potency quite useful to make Elders and Fledgelings more realistic: the older you are - as expressed by your BP - the more powerful you get; but the stronger is your blood - as expressed by your Generation - the higher will be your starting power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 05-04-2023, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T15:46:19-07:00","id":1510725,"title":"","content":"&quot;Realistic&quot; is a strange word to through around to describe the power of fictional monsters at Embrace, and what they can achieve over time.<br /> <br /> The problem is that by trying to have both Generation and Blood Potency the way V5 does, is you really just have a more complicated take on Generation. A 12th Gen vampire in V20 rules has a hard cap on how power they can get no matter how long they endure. A 12th Gen vampire in V5 also has a hard cap of the same sort. The only difference is V20 just has on &quot;level&quot; where V5 has some growth from 1 to 3 before hitting that cap. 7th Gen and lower vampires will always start at where 12th Gens stop, and only grow from there.<br /> <br /> Having a more fluid system isn't inherently bad, but it has to be weighed in whether the increased complexity is really adding to the themes, play experience, and setting of the game. Since V5 wants to keep VtM's &quot;unfair&quot; Generations where power dilutes over time, it shackled Blood Potency to Generation. This undermines a lot of what Blood Potency was meant to do differently for VtR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T03:33:28-07:00","id":1510770,"title":"","content":"There's this phenomenon you can see with history where a rare and horrible crime occurred that sparked public outrage is wrongfully misconstrued by the popular imagination much later to be the norm. For example, people emptying their chamberpots out of the window onto a public street <i>happened</i>, but it certainly wasn't normal and anyone caught doing that would get their head kicked in and delivered to the authorities, but somehow we have it in our minds that it was normal. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GbOKIsMuNWU\" target=\"_blank\">Similarly people have the idea that the ancient Greeks were conspicuous homosexuals who enjoyed teenage boys, when in reality pederasty was a mentor-student relationship with the occasional scandal: <i>Sensational authors, political slander and Translation issues with the greeks frequently using love for strong friendships and brotherly/paternal type love didn't help that case</i>. </a><br /> <br /> I think a lot of V5 changes are extensions of this principle<br /> There are Gehenna cults in the Camarilla, which are persecuted by the establishment: The Camarilla loves Gehenna cults<br /> A few Settites are reactionary purists, despite the ideology of Set being against that kinda thing: Many Settites leave in a schism because there are too many reactionaries. <br /> A lot of Brujah, which is a heavily divided clan internally, don't like the Cam: The Brujah leave the cam. <br /> The princes in many publications are incompetent so we can have a dramatic story: The entire Camarilla is incompetent. <br /> Some Tremere struggle in the pyramid: The Pyramid's divisions were so deep it could split into three big ideologically distinct factions upon leadership loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T09:31:01-07:00","id":1510799,"title":"","content":"For that last I'd expect something very similar to happen in any situation where the Council of Seven are forcibly removed. Without the upper leadership keeping the pyramid organized, many of the egos in middle management would think they were the best candidates to pull the clan together after the disaster, and their rivals being crowned instead would lead to certain ruin. Clan culture doesn't really lend itself to charismatic firebrands and cults of personality (aside from the overall cult). So masterminds who want to draw a following to themselves would need to come up with ideological reasons to choose them rather than leave it up to a choice between a field of backstabby competitors with similar outlooks based on who can offer the most lucrative perks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T13:18:42-07:00","id":1510817,"title":"","content":"I think an important difference between misconceptions about actual history, and how developers look back at RPG settings and where to go forward with them, is that RPG settings are interactive and contemporary. It's entirely possible to have playing the WoD games for years, and come away with the idea that say, the Brujah have no business being a &quot;Cam&quot; Clan and should be predominately Anarchs with a few Cam and Sabbat ones out there, without it being a misconception of the game. It can just be how your play experience has been, and how the play experience of people you talk to has been. Having the personal experience of playing in some differing groups that never really interacted much with each other, I've seen takes on factions/splats get entrenched that aren't in violation of what the books portray, but are more narrow than what the books actually promote at the same time.<br /> <br /> There's also play-style changes that happen when you change things like standard 3-6 player TTRPG to LARPs. When it's just you and your friends, and the ST is tasked with playing the powers of status quo in the setting, everyone being an odd-ball iconoclast is fine. When every member of a city's court but the Prince is a PC, it falls apart. You need the players handling the sheriff, primogen, etc. to all play more to type to keep the game coherent, and there's also just a stronger negative attitude towards &quot;special snowflake&quot; PCs as being disruptive. <br /> <br /> People that have only played TTRPG style with their friends are going to have very different ideas of what the games need to change compared to someone that primarily comes from a large multiple group organized LARP background. Different experiences lead to different expectations of what changes will push play in the direction the new developers actually have as a goal.<br /> <br /> While I bring this up to give an alternative explanation than impact of tunnel-vision on perceptions of history, it's also not a neutral example. I can certainly see a case for having more people with a LARP background bringing in new ideas for a new edition of the WoD, I think a lot of the problems that have divided the community around WoD5 are because WoD5 feels - at least to me - more like LARP folks trying to make a TTRPG without listening to the TTRPG folks. What can be very successful events for major LARP stories, to not necessarily translate well into TTRPG metaplot events.<br /> <br /> Besides divides in the community, I think this extends further because it's not like LARPing or TTRPG styles are actually better for the idea of rebuilding the WoD brand when trying to come up with products in other media spaces. How I would run a WtA LARP vs. how I would run a TTRPG WtA game, is basically orthogonal to what would make a good WtA video game; or what would best update the games for 2020.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T23:11:09-07:00","id":1510862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510799#post1510799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that last I'd expect something very similar to happen in any situation where the Council of Seven are forcibly removed. Without the upper leadership keeping the pyramid organized, many of the egos in middle management would think they were the best candidates to pull the clan together after the disaster, and their rivals being crowned instead would lead to certain ruin. Clan culture doesn't really lend itself to charismatic firebrands and cults of personality (aside from the overall cult). So masterminds who want to draw a following to themselves would need to come up with ideological reasons to choose them rather than leave it up to a choice between a field of backstabby competitors with similar outlooks based on who can offer the most lucrative perks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if every egotistical manager did decide to change things and create rivalries and wars for their leadership bids, it's unlikely that any cultural differences would be significant enough to be noticed by outsiders, and it's unlikely that they'll abandon the Tremere name unless the political situation in their local city demands it (IE it goes anarch or worse) Given Tremere heavily scrutinize embraces to ensure good fits and the usual Tremere paranoia that everything's a plot and the elders know everything any leader that really tries to bring his charges unnecessarily away from Tremere orthodoxy is setting himself up to get replaced by his subordinates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T00:25:33-07:00","id":1510864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510677#post1510677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>VTM</b><br /> <br /> - Anarchs being a sudden uber faction, when they were always the peripheral third faction (clearly someone at Parawolf is an Anarch fan of somesort)<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Sabbat being completely removed from the game as playable characters and lorewise basically all migrating to the Middle-East due to this &quot;Beckoning&quot; plot device nonsense (the most egregious thing Parawolf has done to show their bias against certain elements in the oWoD franchise)<br /> <br /> <br /> - Lasombra mass defecting to the Camarilla despite the Vinculum and the centuries of fighting against the Camarilla, a sect traditionally associated with their greatest rivals, the Venture (no doubt a meta-bias by someone at Parawolf who leaned toward the &quot;Camarilla Lasombra&quot; camp of yore.. that now has become a cringe-worthy reality)<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>partially yeah, martin erricson is a huge anarch fanboy from his larp, looking at some of the writters comments they also identify with them on some level. Its more a general cultural thing at parawolf however. Dissident youth vampires are presumed to be the play norm and that they'd default to anarch. the problem is they've never considered how many assumptions about politics, culture, the fanbase and execution of this idea that this relies on.<br /> <br /> I think they ultimately want the Sabbat to be a pure antagonist faction like nephandi or spirals. The problem is its not particularly clear why the game needs that or how it benifits. Especially as Sabbat players lose out.<br /> <br /> Pretty much yeah, Dawkins has directly commented it was to open lasombra up to carmarilla play more. Which is odd since he knows his lore that carmarilla lasombra have been a thing for decades and since hes a good writter some wwe style plot twist isn't necessary for a number of reasons. I think the idea the lasombra don't belong in the Sabbat (to clarify not they couldnt be elsewhere but that the sabbat is proactively a bad fit) shows a fundementlal misunderstanding of both the clan and the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-06-2023, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T09:02:05-07:00","id":1510884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510864#post1510864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they ultimately want the Sabbat to be a pure antagonist faction like nephandi or spirals. The problem is its not particularly clear why the game needs that or how it benifits. Especially as Sabbat players lose out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it's another one of those things they want to avoid in order to suffer from controversy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:15:13-07:00","id":1510932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510817#post1510817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an important difference between misconceptions about actual history, and how developers look back at RPG settings and where to go forward with them, is that RPG settings are interactive and contemporary. It's entirely possible to have playing the WoD games for years, and come away with the idea that say, the Brujah have no business being a &quot;Cam&quot; Clan and should be predominately Anarchs with a few Cam and Sabbat ones out there, without it being a misconception of the game. It can just be how your play experience has been, and how the play experience of people you talk to has been. Having the personal experience of playing in some differing groups that never really interacted much with each other, I've seen takes on factions/splats get entrenched that aren't in violation of what the books portray, but are more narrow than what the books actually promote at the same time.<br /> <br /> There's also play-style changes that happen when you change things like standard 3-6 player TTRPG to LARPs. When it's just you and your friends, and the ST is tasked with playing the powers of status quo in the setting, everyone being an odd-ball iconoclast is fine. When every member of a city's court but the Prince is a PC, it falls apart. You need the players handling the sheriff, primogen, etc. to all play more to type to keep the game coherent, and there's also just a stronger negative attitude towards &quot;special snowflake&quot; PCs as being disruptive.<br /> <br /> People that have only played TTRPG style with their friends are going to have very different ideas of what the games need to change compared to someone that primarily comes from a large multiple group organized LARP background. Different experiences lead to different expectations of what changes will push play in the direction the new developers actually have as a goal.<br /> <br /> While I bring this up to give an alternative explanation than impact of tunnel-vision on perceptions of history, it's also not a neutral example. I can certainly see a case for having more people with a LARP background bringing in new ideas for a new edition of the WoD, I think a lot of the problems that have divided the community around WoD5 are because WoD5 feels - at least to me - more like LARP folks trying to make a TTRPG without listening to the TTRPG folks. What can be very successful events for major LARP stories, to not necessarily translate well into TTRPG metaplot events.<br /> <br /> Besides divides in the community, I think this extends further because it's not like LARPing or TTRPG styles are actually better for the idea of rebuilding the WoD brand when trying to come up with products in other media spaces. How I would run a WtA LARP vs. how I would run a TTRPG WtA game, is basically orthogonal to what would make a good WtA video game; or what would best update the games for 2020.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting view and one I haven't considered, even with knowing the background of the new people who have been in charge of the WoD IP's. I had bounced off Vampire larps for a a number of reasons and never really cared to indulge in that scene, but there is certainly a different atmosphere and expectations in a tabletop game and in a larp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T00:03:00-07:00","id":1510960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510884#post1510884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose it's another one of those things they want to avoid in order to suffer from controversy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> its a self defeating mindset. No irl events is one thing but if you're removing anything which could be interpreted as controversial in gritty horror game you're going to trim so much off you're playing a hollowed out mess. Furthermore you're Eventually going to tacitly empower bad behaviour in your community since it becomes easy to mask bad faith takes or toxicity. I've seen some real nasty things said about people who like playing Sabbat and para wolf has effectively endorsed that outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 05-07-2023, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T08:17:13-07:00","id":1510983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510960#post1510960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> its a self defeating mindset. No irl events is one thing but if you're removing anything which could be interpreted as controversial in gritty horror game you're going to trim so much off you're playing a hollowed out mess. Furthermore you're Eventually going to tacitly empower bad behaviour in your community since it becomes easy to mask bad faith takes or toxicity. I've seen some real nasty things said about people who like playing Sabbat and para wolf has effectively endorsed that outlook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also don't like it, but It's better lose some players like this making thoses changes than if they suffer legally and the result for the players would be the same at best, at worst they see the franchise as unfeasible and stop everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T08:52:45-07:00","id":1510984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510983#post1510983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also don't like it, but It's better lose some players like this making thoses changes than if they suffer legally and the result for the players would be the same at best, at worst they see the franchise as unfeasible and stop everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suffer legally for making the Sabbat playable? How do you justify that logic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T09:58:11-07:00","id":1510989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510984#post1510984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suffer legally for making the Sabbat playable? How do you justify that logic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask yourself the following question: Is there anything on the Sabbat that could be from some morally questionable/offensive angle or relatable to some hateful group even if in a forced way, which I won't say which because I don't want to get in trouble. I'm going to say yes and that's a loophole for someone to make a legal process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:17:49-07:00","id":1510991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510989#post1510989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask yourself the following question: Is there anything on the Sabbat that could be from some morally questionable/offensive angle or relatable to some hateful group even if in a forced way, which I won't say which because I don't want to get in trouble. I'm going to say yes and that's a loophole for someone to make a legal process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to point out that you're talking about a game where you're playing a bloodsucking manipulative monstrosity that murders hundreds for food and pleasure while turning ordinary humans into addicted pets. That's of course before turning into a wilted callous thing that treats everything in existence as pawns for the express purpose of self aggrandizement . There's more than enough shit for anyone to call this out just for that yet the game is still out.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to play it safe, you wouldn't be pushing these games out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:41:37-07:00","id":1510995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510989#post1510989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask yourself the following question: Is there anything on the Sabbat that could be from some morally questionable/offensive angle or relatable to some hateful group even if in a forced way, which I won't say which because I don't want to get in trouble. I'm going to say yes and that's a loophole for someone to make a legal process.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two people this implication can imply, one I am almost absolutely certain you mean and one who has demonstrable evidence of trying this.<br /> <br /> THe former tends to include a lot of fans of this franchise (and Chronicles, but not our point), because World of Darkness games do a good job of exploring the human condition, building empathy, providing a crash course on how several problems stacked on over large periods of time can create thornsome systems that are hard to remove but do a lot of damage as they remain, and over such things-and in fact, a lot of that crowd arrived at being that crowd because they were introduced to it through these games.<br /> <br /> The latter has tried, and the latter has failed, and that was when World was in the spotlight and even had a murderer inspired by the game as ammo. They have not succeeded, as they have failed to succeed on a lot of different endeavors, and their few successes have done very little and has more revealed the outrage as a combination of spinning wheels and someone milking a moment for cash.<br /> <br /> A little research on the history of games and the sort of outrages you're getting at is very instructive about how and why these things go the way they go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:57:42-07:00","id":1510998,"title":"","content":"I'm struggling to think of anything the Sabbat does that hasn't been farmed out to the Anarchs, Camarilla and Independents in V5........especially with the Tzimisce, Followers of Set..sorry..'Ministry' and Thinblood Squickness being openly playable.<br /> <br /> I mean the Camarilla in V5 is full of Blood Cults that ape or exceed Sabbat Ritae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T11:48:50-07:00","id":1511004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1509297-old-world-of-darkness-is-officially-done?p=1510983#post1510983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also don't like it, but It's better lose some players like this making thoses changes than if they 